On the guardrails, which a licence cannot enforce but an engagement depends on.

This engine proposes; it does not decide. Every output is a proposal for a
named human to accept or reject, and the guardrails that make that true are
structural rather than advisory: no path moves a candidate past Proposed except
a recorded review decision, no score exists without the evidence rows behind
it, drafted text stays marked until a human accepts it, and a synthetic run is
banner-marked wherever it appears.

Removing any of those produces something that looks like this software and is
not it, and nothing in these terms permits presenting it as this engine.

Figures produced from the shipped value assumptions are illustrative. Read
docs/assumptions-register.md before quoting one to a client.
